@@ -76,6 +76,19 @@ baseline_commit: '5b2f627c5708aeb1689133fb5b4ff9b87e0f2bdf'
 - Given an entry is created elsewhere while mounted, when `confirmedWrites` fires, then the chart recomputes without leaving the screen.
 - Given `totals.count > 30`, then exactly 10 bars render regardless of `buckets.length`.

+### Review Findings
+
+- [x] [Review][Patch] Blank-chart defensive guard (`barCounts.isEmpty`) never fires for its own target case — `_condense` always returns exactly 10 elements, and the guard misses the non-empty-but-all-zero case too [dashboard_chart_section.dart:140-156] — fixed: guard now checks `maxCount == 0` (computed after the `totalCount==1`/`>30`/mid-range branch), not `barCounts.isEmpty`.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] `heightFraction` doc comment claims a `.clamp(0,1)` that doesn't exist in code — a negative bucket count could crash via negative `Container` height [dashboard_chart_section.dart:185] — fixed: added `.clamp(0, 1)` to the `heightFraction` expression.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] New VoiceOver announcement for `DashboardCubit` `ResourceError` has no test — a regression would ship silently [account_settings_screen.dart:186-193] — fixed: added a widget test using `interceptAnnouncements`, same pattern as `vault_lock_screen_test.dart`.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] `_condense`'s remainder-absorbing last bar is untested for any non-multiple-of-10 bucket length (incl. the exact length-10 boundary) [dashboard_chart_section.dart:223-248] — fixed: added a 23-bucket remainder-absorption test and an exact-length-10 pass-through test.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] Two spacing values use 8px (`spacingSm`) where the prototype specifies 12px (title→card gap, bar-row→message margin) [dashboard_chart_section.dart:44,193] — fixed: new `DesignTokens.dashboardSectionGap = 12` token, applied in both spots.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] Loading `CircularProgressIndicator` has no semantic label, unlike every other accessibility fix in this commit [dashboard_chart_section.dart:71-76] — fixed: added `semanticsLabel`. (`_errorCard` has no `CircularProgressIndicator` — the original finding's framing was imprecise there; its text is already announced via `AccountSettingsScreen`'s own `_announce`.)
+- [x] [Review][Patch] Misleading DI-ordering comment claims registration call order matters for correctness; only resolution order does [dashboard_injection.dart, injection_container.dart:104] — fixed: both comments reworded to explain `registerLazySingleton`'s lazy-resolution semantics accurately.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] Malformed-response tests only cover a top-level shape mismatch, never a missing required nested field (`totals`, bucket `sources`) [dashboard_remote_data_source_test.dart, dashboard_aggregate_dto_test.dart] — fixed: added a missing-`totals`-field decode test.
+- [x] [Review][Patch] `Expanded`+`SingleChildScrollView` overflow fix is never verified under a constrained viewport or larger text-scale factor [account_settings_screen.dart:457-612] — fixed: added a widget test at a 360×500 viewport with a 2.0 text-scale factor, asserting no `RenderFlex` overflow.
+- [x] [Review][Defer] `DashboardCubit`'s background recompute runs for the whole app session, not just while mounted — every entry created anywhere triggers a live network call even with Configurações closed [dashboard_cubit.dart:26-29] — deferred, pre-existing: faithfully implements the frozen spec's explicit Boundaries directive (`registerLazySingleton` + constructor-subscribe); fixing it means renegotiating frozen spec text, not a code defect.
+
 ## Spec Change Log

 - **Finding (blind-hunter + edge-case-hunter review, confirmed):** the frozen `>30` condensation algorithm ("10 contiguous index chunks, summed count, remainder in the last chunk") degenerates when `bucketCounts.length < 10`: `chunkSize = length ~/ 10 == 0`, so the first 9 chunks each sum an empty range (0) and the 10th chunk absorbs the entire total — renders as 9 invisible bars + 1 full-height bar, defeating the chart's purpose for a plausible user (concentrated activity across fewer than 10 distinct days while exceeding 30 total entries). The shipped implementation was 100% faithful to this frozen text; the defect was in the specified algorithm itself.
